    <string name="skills_how_points">How skill points work. Every finished set earns points: 10 for a basic movement, up to 25 for the hardest. A set counts in full toward its own skill and partly toward the harder skills above it on the same ladder: half, a quarter, then an eighth. Basic strength work adds a little too. Each skill\'s target is what the program gives you before it first asks for that skill, so its points run from 0 to 100 and reach 100 around the day the program gets you there. Repeating a day you have completed adds no points. A group score is the average of the skills the program teaches in Pull, Push, Legs or Core; finish every class and all four reach 100. Difficulty runs from one dot (Beginner, green, taught in Level 1) to five (Elite, red, Level 6 and up).</string>
